  "notes": [
    "Rumoca native simulation with fixed output dt=0.05; OpenModelica dassl with tolerance 1e-8 and 1200 intervals plus event samples. Both detect the EngineOn (fuel_mass>0) and Ascending (v>=0) events; the EngineOn event has an analytic solution t=InitialFuelMass/FuelBurnRate=10 s.",
    "Comparison is on the uniform 0.05 s grid by linear interpolation of both results. OpenModelica's CSV repeats the time stamp exactly at events (3 exact repeats at t = [10.00000000000015, 15.03293294607453, 60.0]); dedupe_last keeps the post-event sample there. Rumoca's output has NO exactly repeated stamps: its pre/post-event sample pairs are strictly increasing and ~1e-13 s apart (auto: 0 exact repeats, 2 near-duplicate pairs, min dt 1.01e-13 s; rk-like: 0 exact repeats, 2 near-duplicate pairs, min dt 5.33e-15 s; bdf: 0 exact repeats, 2 near-duplicate pairs, min dt 1.01e-13 s), so dedupe_last removes nothing from Rumoca output and np.interp works on it directly.",
    "rum.validate reports only a naming-convention warning (lower-case model name 'rocket'); no errors."
  ],
